## composite function

We can combite two (or more) functions by chaining them.

:::definition

Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be functions. A composite function, denoted $f \circ g$, is defined as
\[ (f \circ g)(x)= f(g(x))\]
In other words, we replace $x$ in $f(x)$ by another function $g(x)$.

:::







